\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Minima for the upper bound of $\kappa _0$ in \eqref  {e:kappa_0_practical_upper_bound} for different configurations of $\ensuremath  {\mathbb  {F}}$ (of characteristic $q$ and degree $d$ over its prime field), witness sizes $\ell $, and $\tau $ such that $\ell _1=\ell ^\tau $. By choosing primes in the interval $[2^{a^*}, 2^{128-r_1}]$, we have that the first error term $\kappa _0$ is bounded by the quantity in the $\kappa _0\leq $ column. We include the bits left required to achieve $\kappa _0 < 1/2^{128}$ and the cost of grinding such an amount of bits on a MacBook Air M5 24\,GB multi-threaded, using Blake3 as hash function.}}{80}{table.caption.83}\protected@file@percent }
